Date: Thu, 11 Nov 93 4:43:28 EST
From: rjc@gnu.ai.mit.edu
Subject: META

  Well, I'm sorry to see you leave, however it costs us $20 a month just for
the exi account alone. CPU and bandwidth charges could soar from $50-90 a month
depending on list activity. Harry has been paying out-of-pocket for the
list for the past several months and I'm sure he's down at least $1000
total by now. If you subscribe to extropy, it's $6/yr, that's $0.50 per
month. It costs more in gas to drive to a extropians/cypherpunks meeting.
That $0.50/month is paying to deliver the 50-100k per day that the list
software sends to you, plus cpu charges, plus disk space. I'm sure for poor
students, Max could work out an installment plan. $3 quartly, or $1.5
quarterly for extropy subscribers.

  Are extropians hypocrites? We talk so favorably about capitalism
and commercialization of the internet, but when it comes down to it,
are we unable to recognize or accept the fact that when the government gets 
out of the subsidy business, the net is going to cost us? Perhaps
the Datahighway will be a good thing since universal access will guarantee
that the Extropians List will be subsidized.

  If someone would volunteer to set up a mail-reflector on another site,
people could receive the list for free although they wouldn't be able
to access any of the list's features. Although the mail reflector itself
would incur a yearly charge for bandwidth. 

  I'll admit, I don't like the idea of charging for the list either since
I myself am a poor student who can't even afford many magazine subscriptions,
however, I also don't like the idea of Harry being saddled with the entire
cost of the list, or going with a useless "pledge drive" system where we
beg for yearly fees to keep the list running. Finally, I don't like the
fact that a fee system is going to drive 40-50% of our subscribers off
the list. There's nothing I or ExI can do unless Harry continues his
altruism which I don't think will last much longer.

  Exi-bay will stay up as long as the gnu people let us run it. However,
if the fee system drives a large portion of extropians traffic to exi-bay,
we would eventually be forced to move that to panix also. (meaning
exi-bay bandwidth charges would be billed to your account)

  There is one other solution: someone on the net to lets us
use 20+mb of their internet bandwidth per day plus associated cpu resources
for free.


  I don't know what else to suggest except to shrug and say TANSTAAFL.

-Ray

